66153036911378,"_gp_margin_vs_hist":true,"_score_margin_vs_hist":98.2,"_gate_piotroski":4,"_gp_piotroski":false,"_score_piotroski":44.4,"_gate_spread":null,"_gp_spread":null,"_score_spread":null,"_gate_roic_consistency":null,"_gp_roic_consistency":null,"_score_roic_consistency":null,"_gate_incr_roic":null,"_gp_incr_roic":null,"_score_incr_roic":null,"_gate_margin_advantage":null,"_gp_margin_advantage":null,"_score_margin_advantage":null,"_gate_pool_share":-0.0006136379964687411,"_gp_pool_share":false,"_score_pool_share":39.8,"_gate_rev_durability":null,"_gp_rev_durability":null,"_score_rev_durability":0.0,"_gate_fcf_durability":null,"_gp_fcf_durability":null,"_score_fcf_durability":null,"_gate_margins":null,"_gp_margins":null,"_score_margins":null,"_gate_fund_growth":null,"_gp_fund_growth":null,"_score_fund_growth":null,"_gate_shrhldr_yield":0.027625935831714084,"_gp_shrhldr_yield":true,"_score_shrhldr_yield":41.8,"_gate_share_shrink":0.02286423859939135,"_gp_share_shrink":false,"_score_share_shrink":21.4,"_gate_sbc_dilution":0.01733215932690298,"_gp_sbc_dilution":true,"_score_sbc_dilution":71.1,"_gate_insider_own":0.01192,"_gp_insider_own":false,"_score_insider_own":7.9,"_gate_insider_buying":0.0,"_gp_insider_buying":false,"_score_insider_buying":0.0,"pf":[],"description_full":"First Financial Bancorp. operates as the bank holding company for First Financial Bank that provides commercial banking and banking-related services to individuals and businesses in Ohio, Indiana, Kentucky, and Illinois. The company offers checking and savings accounts; and accepts various deposit products, such as interest-bearing and non-interest-bearing accounts, time deposits, and cash management services for retail and commercial customers. It also provides real estate loans secured by residential property, such as one to four family residential housing units or commercial property comprising owner-occupied and/or investor income producing real estate consisting of apartments, shopping centers, and office buildings; commercial and industrial loans for various purposes, including inventory, receivables, and equipment, as well as equipment and leasehold improvement financing for franchisees; consumer loans, such as new and used vehicle loans, second mortgages on residential real estate and unsecured loans; and home equity lines of credit. In addition, the company offers secured commercial financing services to the insurance industry, registered investment advisors, certified public accountants, indirect auto finance companies, and restaurant franchisees. Further, it provides a range of trust and wealth management services, lease and equipment financing services, currency payments, foreign exchange hedging, commodities hedging, and other advisory products. First Financial Bancorp. was founded in 1863 and is headquartered in Cincinnati, Ohio.","ceo_bio":"Mr. Archie M. Brown Jr. | CEO & Director | Age 64 | Compensation: $1.8M (FY2025)","culture_narrative":"Employs approximately 2K people. Revenue per employee of $400K ranks in the below the sector median among Financial Services peers, improving at 6%/yr \u2014 growing workforce leverage. Each employee generates $141K of free cash flow annually. Stock-based compensation of $7K per employee reflects an ownership culture. CEO compensation is 5\u00d7 revenue per employee (modest relative to workforce productivity). Governance score flags low compensation governance risk (1/10).","financial_summary":["First Financial Bancorp. is a mid-cap financial services business with a $3.4B market cap on $899M of annual revenue.","The top line has compounded at +8% over the past three years, a respectable pace for a business of this size.","Returns on capital run at 7% against a 10% cost of capital, which means the business is destroying value with every dollar it reinvests.","The business throws off $317M in free cash flow \u2014 roughly 35 cents on every revenue dollar, which is the owner-earnings figure that actually belongs to shareholders, and cash conversion sits at 1.32\u00d7 so those profits are backed by real cash.","On the balance sheet, debt is moderate at 3.4\u00d7 net debt/EBITDA, serviceable in normal conditions but worth watching through a downturn, and thin 0.9\u00d7 interest coverage leaves no room for a bad year.","Shareholder yield of 2.8% reflects a genuine commitment to returning capital rather than empire-building, and insider ownership is negligible, so management has little personal stake in the long-term outcome."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Altman Z in the distress zone (0.3) \u2014 the kind of balance-sheet risk that can make a loss permanent","sev":"red","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Low reinvestment-driven growth suggests the compounding engine has stalled","sev":"amber","cat":"growth"},{"text":"Piotroski score 4/9 \u2014 below the median for a healthy business","sev":"amber","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Above-average short interest at 7.4% of float","sev":"amber","cat":"sentiment"},{"text":"Insiders are overwhelmingly selling (100% sell ratio) \u2014 the people who know the business want less of it","sev":"amber","cat":"insider","ratio":0.0},{"text":"Carries more leverage than most Financial Services peers \u2014 a smaller cushion for the inevitable bad year","sev":"amber","cat":"balance_sheet"},{"text":"Above-average market volatility (VIX 26)","sev":"amber","cat":"macro"},{"text":"Late-cycle dynamics increase the probability of a slowdown","sev":"amber","cat":"macro"},{"text":"Credit cycles and regulatory capital \u2014 losses accumulate invisibly in good years and appear all at once, and the time to worry is when underwriting standards are loosest.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"Interest rate regime shifts \u2014 a rapid move in rates can invert the yield curve, crush bond portfolios, and trigger deposit flight simultaneously.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"}],"sector_tailwinds":["37 consecutive years of dividend payments \u2014 an operating record that makes the dividend claim credible","Healthy payout ratio leaves room for both dividend growth and reinvestment"],"news_headlines":[{"title":"FFBC Q3 deep dive: Fee income diversification and C&I lending offset CRE headwinds","source":"finance.yahoo.com","link":"https://finance.yahoo.com/markets/stocks/articles/ffbc-q3-deep-dive-fee-004536909.html","date":"2026-11-03","timestamp":1793666736.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.625,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":["earnings"]},{"title":"First Financial Bancorp (FFBC) Earnings Put Fair Value Back In Focus","source":"simplywall.st","link":"https://simplywall.st/stocks/us/banks/nasdaq-ffbc/first-financial-bancorp/news/first-financial-bancorp-ffbc-earnings-put-fair-value-back-in","date":"2026-11-03","timestamp":1793666110.255,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.908,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":["earnings"]},{"title":"First Financial Bancorp. (NASDAQ:FFBC) Stock Gets Price Target Increase from Truist Financial","source":"thelincolnianonline.com","link":"https://www.thelincolnianonline.com/2026/11/02/first-financial-bancorp-nasdaqffbc-stock-gets-price-target-increase-from-truist-financial.html","date":"2026-11-02","timestamp":1793637418.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.796,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":["analyst_action"]},{"title":"Head-To-Head Comparison: Ponce Financial Group (NASDAQ:PDLB) vs. First Financial Bancorp. (NASDAQ:FFBC)","source":"thelincolnianonline.com","link":"https://www.thelincolnianonline.com/2026/11/01/head-to-head-comparison-ponce-financial-group-nasdaqpdlb-vs-first-financial-bancorp-nasdaqffbc.html","date":"2026-11-01","timestamp":1793541667.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.909,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"Price-Driven Insight from (FFBC) for Rule-Based Strategy","source":"news.stocktradersdaily.com","link":"https://news.stocktradersdaily.com/news_release/24/Price-Driven_Insight_from_FFBC_for_Rule-Based_Strategy_110126052201_1793528521.html","date":"2026-11